list.item:
There are no specific word limits or poetry line limits on fair use. The crucial factors are:


the amount and substantiality of material used in relation to the copyrighted work as a whole;

the effect of the scholar’s use upon the potential market for or value of the copyrighted work—that is, there should be no clear harm to the economic interest of the copyright owner.

Renewed copyrights run an additional 67 years (95 years total), rounded up to the end of the calendar year. Moore’s now-under-copyright volumes come into public domain 95 years after first publication. For example:


Selected Poems (1935)—in public domain as of 2030;

What Are Years (1941)—in public domain as of 2036;

Collected Poems (1951)—in public domain as of 2046.
